1
00:00:01,181 --> 00:00:09,221
The Princess Sapphire

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Princess Knight,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,107 --> 00:01:50,147
Forty-Second Episode
The Rat Man

15
00:02:08,501 --> 00:02:10,731
Many happy returns of the day, friend!

16
00:02:11,141 --> 00:02:13,336
Long live the harvest festival!

17
00:02:28,861 --> 00:02:31,421
These fireworks are magnificent.

18
00:02:33,101 --> 00:02:35,171
Oh, how beautiful!

19
00:02:36,181 --> 00:02:38,490
They are celebrating the wheat harvest.

20
00:02:38,741 --> 00:02:41,574
Yeah! This year was excellent!
But where are you going?

21
00:02:42,501 --> 00:02:45,857
- I’d like to go down into town.
- Wait, I’m coming with you.

22
00:02:46,181 --> 00:02:48,456
Just a minute, time to change my clothes.

23
00:02:53,101 --> 00:02:55,820
But...! What a struggle! Are
you coming in that outfit?

24
00:02:55,861 --> 00:02:58,011
Why?
Don't tell me you don't like it!

25
00:03:04,541 --> 00:03:07,055
Long live Silverland! Hurrah!

26
00:03:17,821 --> 00:03:20,051
I've never seen such a rich harvest!

27
00:03:20,101 --> 00:03:22,740
- Let's have a little drink to it!
- Yeah!

28
00:03:22,941 --> 00:03:25,614
Hey, the mice harvest is rich too!

29
00:03:37,421 --> 00:03:40,174
Help!

30
00:03:42,901 --> 00:03:45,654
The mice! Help!

31
00:03:51,541 --> 00:03:55,011
- So many mice!
- Damn! But how many are there?!

32
00:04:06,101 --> 00:04:09,491
My dear little mice, this year
the granaries of Silverland...

33
00:04:09,541 --> 00:04:11,930
...are full of excellent wheat!

34
00:04:12,141 --> 00:04:14,701
Devour as much as you want!

35
00:04:19,541 --> 00:04:22,101
Help! Help!

36
00:04:23,821 --> 00:04:26,210
Quick! Let's run!

37
00:04:44,861 --> 00:04:47,250
Where are all these mice coming from?

38
00:04:53,701 --> 00:04:56,818
Look there!
They’ve eaten all the wheat!

39
00:04:57,061 --> 00:05:00,610
We won't have anything left
to eat until the next harvest.

40
00:05:00,661 --> 00:05:02,856
How will we manage to get by?

41
00:05:02,901 --> 00:05:06,735
Just this year, when the harvest
had been most abundant..!

42
00:05:07,421 --> 00:05:09,935
We don't even have
seeds to plant!

43
00:05:09,981 --> 00:05:13,257
If something doesn't happen,
we'll all starve to death!

44
00:05:13,301 --> 00:05:15,019
That's for sure!

45
00:05:15,061 --> 00:05:18,770
I've never seen so many rats in
my life! Where could they have come from?

46
00:05:25,701 --> 00:05:29,774
Did you see the commotion in the
village over those rats, Grand Duke?

47
00:05:29,821 --> 00:05:32,813
They said that all
the grain has been plundered.

48
00:05:33,181 --> 00:05:36,810
An excellent move! That man
with the rats is very powerful,

49
00:05:36,861 --> 00:05:40,171
just as an agent
of Union X should be.

50
00:05:40,741 --> 00:05:44,814
That way, when Union X attacks
our kingdom to subjugate it,

51
00:05:45,021 --> 00:05:47,012
they will succeed with great ease.

52
00:05:47,061 --> 00:05:49,291
Yes, they'll be too hungry
to run away!

53
00:05:55,141 --> 00:05:58,019
I am a messenger
from the Sovereign of Goldland!

54
00:05:58,061 --> 00:06:00,416
I have a message
for His Majesty the King!

55
00:06:00,461 --> 00:06:02,656
A message
from the Sovereign of Goldland?!

56
00:06:11,221 --> 00:06:13,496
Listen!
The King of Goldland,

57
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:16,533
informed of the calamity that
has befallen our kingdom,

58
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:18,890
has offered
to lend us some grain!

59
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:22,373
Our Sovereign, who does
not want his subjects to suffer...

60
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:26,494
neither hunger nor famine, has
accepted the King of Goldland’s offer!

61
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:29,460
- Hurrah!
- Hooray!

62
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:32,378
How kind of the King of Goldland!

63
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:34,651
Our granaries will be full again!

64
00:06:49,060 --> 00:06:51,052
Let's see.

65
00:06:56,340 --> 00:06:58,218
Heavenly Father, forgive me!

66
00:06:58,260 --> 00:07:00,855
I'm too hungry
to be able to fall asleep.

67
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:06,018
I hope you won't be too angry
with me if I take something to eat.

68
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:15,018
Where are Duralumin and Nylon
going in the middle of the night?

69
00:07:40,340 --> 00:07:42,297
Hello!

70
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:45,490
I'm happy to see you.

71
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:48,657
Are you about to sit down to eat?

72
00:07:49,740 --> 00:07:52,619
Yes! And I would be delighted
if you would have lunch with me.

73
00:07:52,660 --> 00:07:55,129
Thank you,
you are very kind indeed!

74
00:07:56,180 --> 00:07:59,014
What a delicious smell! What is it?

75
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:02,099
It's a soup of worms,
centipedes, and spiders.

76
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:06,089
This fry-up looks tasty.
What is it?

77
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:08,211
It's a toad omelet.

78
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:13,012
- Would you like some caterpillar soup?
- No, thank you..!

79
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:16,174
Am I wrong, or do you not like
my cooking very much?

80
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:18,530
Perhaps you would only like some liqueur?

81
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:22,140
- Yes, we'd prefer that!
- We like liqueur very much!

82
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:26,411
Good! It's truly delicious!

83
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:30,577
You like it, eh? It's distilled
bat blood.

84
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:37,538
Guys, not like that!
Remember that I'm eating lunch!

85
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:40,337
Forgive us, but we wanted to tell you...

86
00:08:40,380 --> 00:08:43,020
...that, after your little job
of making all the grain disappear,

87
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:46,656
the King of Goldland has offered
to refill the empty granaries.

88
00:08:46,701 --> 00:08:49,738
Don't worry! I will make sure
that not a single grain...

89
00:08:49,781 --> 00:08:52,170
...can reach Silverland!

90
00:08:52,221 --> 00:08:55,019
Will you manage to destroy
that grain too?

91
00:08:55,421 --> 00:08:57,810
Certainly! After all,
the time has come again...

92
00:08:57,861 --> 00:09:00,295
...to feed
my dear little mice!

93
00:09:04,701 --> 00:09:07,295
Thank you, dear,
for your long journey.

94
00:09:11,541 --> 00:09:15,454
They inform me that the wheat wagons
will leave Goldland tomorrow morning,

95
00:09:15,501 --> 00:09:17,890
led by Prince Franz.

96
00:09:20,301 --> 00:09:23,213
And at what point do you intend
to have them attacked?

97
00:09:23,261 --> 00:09:26,219
Once past the border, the wagons
will take the shortest route...

98
00:09:26,261 --> 00:09:28,331
...to reach
Silverland Castle.

99
00:09:28,381 --> 00:09:30,497
I will wait for them near the river...

100
00:09:30,541 --> 00:09:33,851
...and every grain of wheat
will end up as food for my mice.

101
00:09:34,701 --> 00:09:38,011
What if the tanks took
the other road, the one to the West?

102
00:09:38,061 --> 00:09:41,736
It won't happen! It would be madness
to send the tanks down that road.

103
00:09:41,781 --> 00:09:45,410
In fact, not only is it very long,
but it is also a mountain road:

104
00:09:45,461 --> 00:09:49,215
in many stretches it is so narrow
that a tank would barely fit through.

105
00:09:49,261 --> 00:09:52,014
No, friends!
I know where to wait for those tanks!

106
00:09:52,061 --> 00:09:54,211
Yes, I think you're right.

107
00:09:55,181 --> 00:09:58,810
You truly deserve to be
Mr. X's right-hand man!

108
00:10:06,741 --> 00:10:08,891
F... F... Friend, stay calm!

109
00:10:09,301 --> 00:10:12,338
I must give him something..
Here, take this! You'll like this!

110
00:10:14,941 --> 00:10:17,660
Hey, my children!
I have guests with me!

111
00:10:17,701 --> 00:10:19,817
Will you stop fighting?!

112
00:10:26,701 --> 00:10:28,578
What?! Are you serious?

113
00:10:28,621 --> 00:10:31,010
Yes! Hurry up or something
terrible will happen!

114
00:10:31,061 --> 00:10:32,892
I'm coming right away!

115
00:10:39,701 --> 00:10:41,896
Sapphire, hurry up!

116
00:10:46,941 --> 00:10:49,580
Sapphire, take me with you!

117
00:10:49,781 --> 00:10:53,615
Damn! Every time she's about to
meet Franz, she loses her head!

118
00:11:09,341 --> 00:11:11,855
Now, my dear little mice,
come with me!

119
00:11:11,901 --> 00:11:14,893
I will feed you the
tasty grain of Goldland!

120
00:11:14,941 --> 00:11:17,409
Get ready
for another good feast!

121
00:11:19,101 --> 00:11:21,012
Let's go!

122
00:11:44,181 --> 00:11:46,649
Prince, we are ready!

123
00:11:47,901 --> 00:11:50,369
Good! I will bring
this grain to Silverland.

124
00:11:50,421 --> 00:11:52,889
Whatever happens,
nothing will stop me!

125
00:11:54,861 --> 00:11:57,136
- Let's go!
- Forward!

126
00:12:21,621 --> 00:12:25,011
Faster! Keep the horses moving!

127
00:12:25,061 --> 00:12:28,815
I fear it will be a tiring journey.
We have a long way to go.

128
00:12:59,221 --> 00:13:01,337
Greetings to you, mysterious knight!

129
00:13:01,381 --> 00:13:04,373
Prince Franz, Princess
Sapphire sends you this.

130
00:13:05,021 --> 00:13:07,171
Oh, Sapphire...

131
00:13:10,141 --> 00:13:12,177
What? She tells me to stop?!

132
00:13:12,221 --> 00:13:15,930
Prince, this is an opportunity
to get rid of all those mice.

133
00:13:15,981 --> 00:13:17,972
We will set a trap for them!

134
00:13:18,221 --> 00:13:20,212
I agree!

135
00:13:30,621 --> 00:13:34,011
Listen to me carefully! I will
show you what you have to do.

136
00:13:35,101 --> 00:13:37,740
Remember to do
exactly what I said.

137
00:13:37,781 --> 00:13:39,453
You must not make a mistake!

138
00:13:40,221 --> 00:13:42,894
Yes, I believe this
plan can work.

139
00:13:43,821 --> 00:13:46,096
Your task will be very delicate.

140
00:13:46,901 --> 00:13:50,211
Everything is ready! Let's
get ready to spring the trap!

141
00:14:00,461 --> 00:14:03,737
Tonight, my dear little
mice will give a hard time...

142
00:14:03,781 --> 00:14:07,217
...to that fool Prince
Franz! It will be fun!

143
00:14:19,181 --> 00:14:21,331
Keep up this pace!

144
00:14:24,821 --> 00:14:28,416
My dear little mice, all the
grain in those wagons is for you!

145
00:14:48,741 --> 00:14:52,256
Go, my children! Loot!
Destroy! Devour!

146
00:14:52,301 --> 00:14:54,895
And let not even a grain
of that wheat remain!

147
00:15:04,741 --> 00:15:06,732
Something is wrong!

148
00:15:07,421 --> 00:15:10,060
What?! They’re just mannequins!

149
00:15:15,221 --> 00:15:18,577
This is gunpowder! And here
there are barrels full of oil!

150
00:15:19,021 --> 00:15:21,581
Curse it,
they’ve set a trap for us!

151
00:15:24,181 --> 00:15:26,297
Shoot the arrows at the wagons!

152
00:15:32,021 --> 00:15:33,693
Dammit!

153
00:15:41,621 --> 00:15:44,533
Oh, no! My dear little mice!

154
00:15:46,621 --> 00:15:48,339
Dammit!

155
00:15:53,181 --> 00:15:56,298
An opening!
This way!

156
00:15:56,541 --> 00:15:58,896
Come,
you who are survivors!

157
00:16:00,461 --> 00:16:03,692
Poor dears! Forgive me!
I was a fool...

158
00:16:03,741 --> 00:16:06,175
...to let you end up
in this trap!

159
00:16:12,501 --> 00:16:14,696
It's time! Cut the ropes!

160
00:16:29,221 --> 00:16:34,056
Cursed Franz! I will remember
you! One day I will have my revenge!

161
00:16:57,301 --> 00:16:59,178
Here are the wagons!

162
00:17:05,101 --> 00:17:08,855
They are preparing an
ambush, exactly as I expected.

163
00:17:16,021 --> 00:17:18,012
Forward, attack!

164
00:17:30,581 --> 00:17:32,936
There’s a landslide! Stop the wagons!

165
00:17:41,261 --> 00:17:44,651
Damn that mysterious
knight! I’ll show him!

166
00:17:49,501 --> 00:17:51,139
Hurray, I hit him!

167
00:17:51,181 --> 00:17:54,218
Forward, let’s attack
him! Finish him! Finish him!

168
00:17:55,621 --> 00:17:57,339
Who is there?

169
00:17:57,541 --> 00:17:59,896
Ready? Shoot!

170
00:17:59,941 --> 00:18:02,011
Help! Help!

171
00:18:02,701 --> 00:18:04,692
Are you alright, mysterious knight?

172
00:18:04,741 --> 00:18:06,697
Yes, nothing serious.
It's only a scratch.

173
00:18:06,741 --> 00:18:08,811
Thank you from the bottom of my heart for saving me

174
00:18:09,021 --> 00:18:12,013
No, it is I who must be grateful for your help.

175
00:18:12,301 --> 00:18:14,417
But what is the matter? Are you unwell?

176
00:18:14,901 --> 00:18:17,574
- It's nothing. - I'll have your wound treated immediately!

177
00:18:17,621 --> 00:18:20,499
No, thank you, I'm fine!
Goodbye, Prince!

178
00:18:21,101 --> 00:18:23,012
See you soon!

179
00:18:26,021 --> 00:18:28,012
What a strange knight...!

180
00:18:29,021 --> 00:18:32,331
- It's the grain wagons!
- Long live Prince Franz!

181
00:18:56,221 --> 00:18:59,850
He loves me not, he loves me, he loves me not.

182
00:19:04,541 --> 00:19:06,611
Oh! This is Sapphire!

183
00:19:08,021 --> 00:19:10,216
Forgive me for keeping you waiting.

184
00:19:11,181 --> 00:19:13,490
What is that bandage? Are you hurt?

185
00:19:15,021 --> 00:19:17,410
yes...
No, well, it was a thorn

186
00:19:17,461 --> 00:19:19,577
I hurt myself on the stem of a rose.

187
00:19:20,101 --> 00:19:22,615
A rose that has hurt your delightful little arm...

188
00:19:22,661 --> 00:19:25,175
...does not deserve to be a flower.
I want to cut it down!

189
00:19:25,221 --> 00:19:26,813
How kind you are..

190
00:19:26,861 --> 00:19:29,011
- Princess Sapphire.
- Franz..!

191
00:19:51,341 --> 00:19:54,174
Finally we are face to face, Prince Franz!

192
00:19:55,501 --> 00:19:57,173
I will have no mercy!

193
00:19:57,461 --> 00:19:59,452
Sapphire, throw me the sword!

194
00:20:14,501 --> 00:20:16,332
Damn it!

195
00:20:27,901 --> 00:20:30,461
- You're trapped!
- Damn it!

196
00:20:30,781 --> 00:20:34,137
- Surrender, if you value your life!
- Dammit!

197
00:20:36,621 --> 00:20:39,215
Now talk! Tell us who you really are!

198
00:20:39,341 --> 00:20:41,901
Why did you attack me?
What were you trying to do?

199
00:20:43,381 --> 00:20:45,770
I wanted to avenge the mice you killed!

200
00:20:45,821 --> 00:20:47,652
Those dear little animals of mine!

201
00:20:47,901 --> 00:20:49,493
The mice?

202
00:20:51,621 --> 00:20:55,819
We're sorry, but this time
you'll have to let our friend go.

203
00:20:56,021 --> 00:20:58,137
This guy is a friend of yours?

204
00:20:58,181 --> 00:21:01,014
Are you saying the two of you
have allied yourselves with him?

205
00:21:01,701 --> 00:21:04,773
Certainly!
I had requested his help.

206
00:21:04,821 --> 00:21:08,370
.. ...to have the mice invade the
town and thus take possession of it!

207
00:21:12,541 --> 00:21:16,011
- Goodbye! - What?!
- Hey, where are you going?

208
00:21:16,181 --> 00:21:19,412
Now that the plan has failed, I have
nothing more to do with you,

209
00:21:19,461 --> 00:21:21,850
so I'm going to Mr. X
to inform him!

210
00:21:22,221 --> 00:21:24,212
Don't be a fool!

211
00:21:24,381 --> 00:21:27,453
- Goodbye!
- Wait! Wait!

212
00:21:32,581 --> 00:21:35,334
I remember that I have something
very urgent to do!

213
00:21:35,381 --> 00:21:37,212
Bastard!

214
00:21:41,101 --> 00:21:42,659
No!

215
00:21:44,101 --> 00:21:47,491
You were very good, Franz, at
giving those two a good lesson.

216
00:21:47,541 --> 00:21:50,419
You know, I believe they
won't forget it for a long while

217
00:21:50,741 --> 00:21:54,097
We were lucky.
Union X will be discouraged now.

218
00:21:54,741 --> 00:21:57,892
It was a great feat
to defeat the rat man.

219
00:22:37,661 --> 00:22:40,812
You know what?
If you are always close,

220
00:22:40,861 --> 00:22:43,694
you will be so strong
as to overcome all adversity!

221
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:25,000
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

222
00:23:25,001 --> 00:23:28,361
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

223
00:23:28,362 --> 00:23:32,132
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

224
00:23:32,133 --> 00:23:35,294
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

225
00:23:35,295 --> 00:23:39,108
♪ Sen'nen man'nen hyakuman-nen ♪
A thousand years, ten thousand years, a million years,

226
00:23:39,109 --> 00:23:42,405
♪ Ribbon de tsunagou ichioku-nen ♪
Let’s connect with ribbons for a billion years!

227
00:23:42,406 --> 00:23:46,411
♪ Akuma ga kute mo arashi ga kute mo ♪
Even if devils come, even if storms arrive,

228
00:23:46,412 --> 00:23:49,850
♪ tsunaida kokoro wa hanarenai ♪
Our bonded hearts will never part.

229
00:23:49,851 --> 00:23:53,471
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

230
00:23:53,472 --> 00:23:56,832
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

231
00:23:56,833 --> 00:24:00,603
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

232
00:24:00,604 --> 00:24:03,765
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

233
00:24:03,789 --> 00:24:15,336
